{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1522366955,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMDk5MzY3MjU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2364","origin":"github"},"title":"Make our silent UIs (e.g. SilentConsoleLog) provide \".question\"","message":"#### What is the problem?\nATM non interactive UIs simply do not implement the requiring interaction `.question`, and whenever non-interactive UI is used (e.g. in the tests) and code didn't explicitly check for e.g. having credentials available, it would fail with a non-informative \n```\n'SilentConsoleLog' object has no attribute 'question'\n```\n\nI think they should provide .question which would just blow with a summary -- the question, so we at least know what code triggered the blow","files":null}]}